# Production configuration, baked into the bundle at build time.
#
# WHY A KEY IS COMMITTED HERE, AND WHY THAT IS NOT A MISTAKE
#
# A Supabase publishable key is public by design. It ships inside the
# JavaScript of every Supabase app, so anyone can read it with view-source.
# Keeping it out of git would add deployment friction and protect nothing.
#
# It is safe because it grants no authority. Every rule is enforced by row
# level security in Postgres, and that was verified against this exact key
# rather than assumed. Holding it, an anonymous caller can:
#
#     file a pending report            201, allowed and intended
#     insert a pre-approved report     401, blocked
#     read a pending report            [], invisible
#     approve any report               [], zero rows changed
#     delete any report                zero rows, no delete policy exists
#     upload a non-JPEG                400, bucket rejects the mime type
#     report a coordinate outside      400, CHECK constraint rejects it
#
# NEVER put the service_role key in this file, or in any file under
# frontend/. That one bypasses every policy above and is a real secret.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://rrvtuzjuukxizmlgqbnn.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_zaSPTPmtbn-HkLGJFujM7Q_9fdV-gnv
